{%- comment -%}
  CAVIERA compact loader — the same Living Oryx video, small and restrained, for component-level
  async waits (cart drawer updates, predictive search, add to bag, form submission) — never a
  generic spinner, per brief ("the universal CAVIERA loading language").

  Purely decorative (aria-hidden) — the host component keeps its own existing aria-live/aria-busy/
  status semantics for the actual accessible announcement; this only adds the visual.

  Caller controls visibility with its own CSS (typically an ancestor `.is-loading` class revealing
  this via a plain descendant selector — see assets/caviera-loader.css, .caviera-loader-inline, and
  each call site's own small CSS rule) — this snippet only renders the inert markup.

  Params:
    size:  optional pixel width (default 56px, see --loader-inline-size below)
    class: optional extra class(es) on the root <span>, for a call-site-specific CSS hook
{%- endcomment -%}
<span
  class="caviera-loader-inline{% if class %} {{ class }}{% endif %}"
  data-caviera-loader-inline
  aria-hidden="true"
  {%- if size %} style="--loader-inline-size: {{ size }}px;"{% endif %}
>
  <video
    class="caviera-loader-inline__video"
    autoplay
    muted
    loop
    playsinline
    preload="none"
  >
    <source src="{{ 'caviera-loader-oryx-2026.mp4' | asset_url }}" type="video/mp4">
  </video>
</span>
